{
  "date": "2026-10-19",
  "base_commit": "ec16e65df7f3863bf4e6fbff5d3beffa0a6aa271",
  "scope": "One existing non-main research paper updated; promoted main papers and Lean sources unchanged.",
  "new_results": [
    "Every finite width: learning from actual normalized raw target cost a_N, with a universal polynomial prefactor times exp(C sqrt(L(a_N-V*)_+)).",
    "Finite-N collective exceptional-prior-mass bound via forward exchangeable entropy decrement, projected readout entropy, approximate covariance paths and local representability.",
    "Quantitative Gaussian target-mass lower bounds for Fourier seeds and bounded threshold-circuit teachers, obtained by bounded-score scalar-channel tracking and deterministic rare gate groups.",
    "Every realizable width: polynomial samples for all parities and Fourier-variation targets at logarithmic minimum learner depth; R^{O(D+1)} samples for bounded-weight tanh teachers at L >= C(D+1)log R.",
    "Every realizable width: R^{O(h)} samples for arbitrary-real-weight Boolean threshold teachers, independent of coefficient magnitudes and precision; halfspaces have polynomial samples at every N >= 1.",
    "Every realizable width: polynomial bounds for fixed-rank input bottlenecks, two-state branching programs and bounded-derived-length solvable-group programs, including width-four permutation programs.",
    "Improved Boolean blocking and quasipolynomial formula bounds, distinguishing the optimized rate-only parameter from the proved finite-width parameter."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Joint polynomial sample complexity in arbitrary teacher width and depth remains open; the general teacher exponent grows with depth.",
    "The target-class results retain explicit minimum learner-depth conditions and require realizability at the learner width.",
    "The learner retains global all-input output margins, iid noiseless labels and exact training fit.",
    "The construction does not quantify convergence within a specified error to the optimal limiting rate of an arbitrary target.",
    "No bound on compressed weight product or precision, and no efficient posterior-sampling algorithm, is claimed.",
    "Independent mathematical AI-agent audits and reproducible PDF builds are not Lean verification."
  ],
